{
  "slug": "artist:elvis-presley",
  "name": "Elvis Presley",
  "editorial_article": "Elvis Presley was an American musician and one of the most influential cultural figures of the 20th century. Rising to prominence in the mid-1950s, he became a global phenomenon, bridging genres such as rock 'n' roll, pop, and country. His career began in earnest with his first commercial single, 'That's All Right', in 1954, followed by his self-titled debut album in 1956. Over the course of his career, Presley achieved unprecedented commercial success, with estimates suggesting he has sold up to 500 million records worldwide. He remains a record-holding artist in the United States, recognized by the RIAA for having the most certified albums and total certifications of any artist in history.\n\nBeyond his initial chart dominance, Presley's legacy is maintained through extensive catalog releases, including the Follow That Dream (FTD) collector's label established in 1999. This label provides dedicated fans with rare session outtakes, soundboard concert recordings, and deluxe reissues of his classic albums. His influence continues to be measured by music historians and organizations like Billboard, which ranks him among the greatest artists of all time. His holiday release, 'Elvis' Christmas Album', stands as the highest-selling Christmas album in history, cementing his status as a perennial force in popular music.",
